      "text": "Let $b$ be the weight of one bowling ball and $c$ be the weight of one canoe. From the problem, we have the following two equations: \\[\n7b = 3c \\quad \\text{(1)} \\] \\[\n2c = 56 \\quad \\text{(2)} \n\\] We can substitute the value of $c$ from equation (2) into equation (1) to find the value of $b$: \\[\n7b = 3 \\cdot \\frac{56}{2} \\implies 7b = 84 \\implies b = \\frac{84}{7} = 12 \n\\] Therefore, one bowling ball weighs $\\boxed{12 \\text{ pounds}}$.",
